      "text": "First, we need to find the projection point. The projection is given by:\n\\[\n\\proj_{\\mathbf{a}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}}{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}} \\mathbf{a},\n\\]\nwhere $\\mathbf{a}$ is the vector onto which we are projecting. In this problem, $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nThe dot product $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}$ is:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z.\n\\]\n\nThe dot product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}$ is:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35.\n\\]\n\nSo the projection is:\n\\[\n\\proj_{\\mathbf{a}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nWe are given that this projection is equal to $\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix},$ so:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nEquating the two components, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}.\n\\]\n\nSolving for $z,$ we multiply both sides by 35:\n\\[\n15 - z = 12.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, $z = \\boxed{3}.$",
