      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(z\\) such that the projection of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we start by recalling the formula for the projection of vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The projection is given as \n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these results into the projection formula:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\mathbf{b} = \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nWe get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nEquating the scalar components (which are identical):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\cdot -3 = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3(15 - z)}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3(15 - z) = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 4\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\nz = 15 - 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz = 11\n\\]\n\nSo the value of \\(z\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
